    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "$ABCD$ is a rectangle that is four times as long as it is wide. Point $E$ is the midpoint of $\\overline{BC}$. What percent of the rectangle is shaded?\n\n[asy]\ndraw( (0,0) -- (4,0) -- (4,1) -- (0,1) -- cycle);draw( (2,0) -- (0,1) ); draw( (4,0) -- (0,1));\nfill( (0,0) -- (0,1) -- (2,0) -- cycle, gray); fill( (0,1) -- (4,0) -- (4,1) -- cycle, gray);\nlabel(\"$A$\", (0,1) , NW); label(\"$B$\", (0,0) , SW); label(\"$C$\", (4,0) , SE);label(\"$D$\", (4,1) , NE);label(\"$E$\", (2,0), S);\n[/asy]\n\nThink step by step inside <think> </think> tags, then give your final answer inside \\boxed{}."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To determine what percent of the rectangle is shaded, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Define the dimensions of the rectangle:**\n   Let the width of the rectangle \\(ABCD\\) be \\(w\\). Since the rectangle is four times as long as it is wide, the length of the rectangle is \\(4w\\).\n\n2. **Identify the coordinates of the vertices:**\n   Place the rectangle in the coordinate plane with \\(A\\) at \\((0, 1)\\), \\(B\\) at \\((0, 0)\\), \\(C\\) at \\((4w, 0)\\), and \\(D\\) at \\((4w, 1)\\).\n\n3. **Locate point \\(E\\):**\n   Point \\(E\\) is the midpoint of \\(\\overline{BC}\\). Since \\(B\\) is at \\((0, 0)\\) and \\(C\\) is at \\((4w, 0)\\), the coordinates of \\(E\\) are:\n   \\[\n   E = \\left( \\frac{0 + 4w}{2}, \\frac{0 + 0}{2} \\right) = (2w, 0)\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine the area of the shaded regions:**\n   - The shaded region is a triangle formed by points \\(A\\), \\(E\\), and \\(D\\).\n   - The base of this triangle is the width of the rectangle, \\(w\\).\n   - The height of the triangle is the length of the rectangle, \\(4w\\).\n\n5. **Calculate the area of the triangle:**\n   The area \\(A\\) of a triangle is given by:\n   \\[\n   A = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height}\n   \\]\n   Substituting the base and height:\n   \\[\n   A = \\frac{1}{2} \\times w \\times 4w = 2w^2\n   \\]\n\n6. **Calculate the area of the rectangle:**\n   The area \\(A_{\\text{rectangle}}\\) of the rectangle is:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{rectangle}} = \\text{length} \\times \\text{width} = 4w \\times w = 4w^2\n   \\]\n\n7. **Determine the percentage of the rectangle that is shaded:**\n   The percentage of the rectangle that is shaded is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Percentage} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{Area of the shaded triangle}}{\\text{Area of the rectangle}} \\right) \\times 100\\%\n   \\]\n   Substituting the areas:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Percentage} = \\left( \\frac{2w^2}{4w^2} \\right) \\times 100\\% = \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\right) \\times 100\\% = 50\\%\n   \\]\n\nThus, the percent of the rectangle that is shaded is \\(\\boxed{50}\\)."
